; DOMAIN: mathematics/number-theory/class-field-theory [CLOSED, derived 2026-08-01]; Claim: Class field theory describes abelian extensions of number fields and local fields via the Artin reciprocity map. Key results: the Artin map from the idele class group to the Galois group of the maximal abelian extension is surjective with kernel the connected component; Kronecker-Weber theorem (every finite abelian extension of Q is contained in a cyclotomic field); Hilbert class field (maximal unramified abelian extension, Galois group isomorphic to the ideal class group); local class field theory via the local Artin map from K* to Gal(K^ab/K); the reciprocity law relating Frobenius elements to ideles; and the existence theorem classifying abelian extensions by norm groups. Bridges to automorphic_forms (Artin reciprocity as GL(1) Langlands), zeta_function (Dedekind zeta residues and class number formula), and algebraic_number_theory.;; Artin reciprocity map: surjective homomorphism from idele class group to Galois group of maximal abelian extension, kernel is connected component
(|- ((==> (&& (--> NumberField $K) (--> IdeleClassGroup $C_K) (--> GaloisGroup $G (MaximalAbelianExtension $K)) (--> Surjective $art $C_K $G) (--> Kernel $art (ConnectedComponent $C_K)))) (--> ArtinReciprocity $K $art)) (stv 1.0 0.9))
;; Kronecker-Weber theorem: every finite abelian extension of Q is contained in a cyclotomic field
(|- ((==> (&& (--> FiniteAbelianExtension $L $Q))) (--> Exists $n (CyclotomicField $n (Contains $L)))) (stv 1.0 0.9))
